<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Piedras Negras</h1><p class="st-meta">460 CE – 808 CE (approx.) · capital Piedras Negras</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Classic Maya kingdom on the Usumacinta whose stelae enabled Tatiana Proskouriakoff to prove in 1960 that Maya inscriptions record real history.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Piedras Negras, anciently Yo'k'ib', occupied the Guatemalan bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usumacinta-river">Usumacinta</a>, upstream from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yaxchilan">Yaxchilan</a>. Its kings appear in inscriptions from the 5th century, around 460 CE, and the city fought long wars with Yaxchilan over the river valley.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From the early 7th century its rulers raised a series of stelae marking accessions, showing a king seated in a niche above a ladder. Analysing these sequences, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatiana-proskouriakoff">Proskouriakoff</a> demonstrated that the glyphs named rulers and dated events in their lives. The kingdom was often allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaan">Kingdom of Kaan</a> and built sweat baths, palaces and a fine carved throne.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 808 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yaxchilan">Yaxchilan</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-yat-ahk-ii">K'inich Yat Ahk II</a>, the last known king, and the city declined swiftly, being abandoned by the early 9th century. Excavations in the 1930s and 1990s revealed much of its layout.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 460 CE – 808 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.86%;width:6.93%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>460 CE – 808 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Piedras Negras</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>K'inich Yo'nal Ahk I, Itzamnaaj K'awiil, K'inich Yat Ahk II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Yokib, Yo'k'ib'</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=634&amp;focus=piedras-negras" aria-label="Piedras Negras on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2199 1540 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Piedras Negras lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2519 1796L2525 1806"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2525 1806h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2519 1796h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2519 1796h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Piedras Negras. <a href="/atlas?year=634&amp;focus=piedras-negras">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

